1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,726
Python tuples,

2
00:00:01,776 --> 00:00:04,200
explained in six steps.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,609
A tuple is a fixed

4
00:00:07,659 --> 00:00:10,200
group of values.

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,138
Read items by position,

6
00:00:13,188 --> 00:00:16,200
negative counts from the end.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,166
A slice gives you

8
00:00:19,216 --> 00:00:22,200
a new, smaller tuple.

9
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,186
count() tells how many times

10
00:00:26,236 --> 00:00:28,200
a value appears.

11
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,450
Unpacking splits a tuple

12
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,200
into separate variables.

13
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,327
Tuples are immutable:

14
00:00:37,377 --> 00:00:40,200
you cannot change them.

15
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,288
Save this cheat sheet

16
00:00:43,338 --> 00:00:46,600
and follow for more Python!
